{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 63, :comments ["<b>To meditate in the field.</b> To walk among the shrubs — that is, to delight and stroll among the trees in the cool of the day. This is the plain sense." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'To meditate in the field' — שיחה is nothing but prayer, as it is said (Psalms 102:1): ״תפלה לעני כי יעטוף ולפני ה׳ ישפוך שיחו״. And from here our Rabbis, blessed be their memory, said: Isaac established the prayer of Minḥah." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> 'To meditate in the field' — he who prays by means of the Unique Name invokes the pronoun, and through the pronoun finds Him going out. And this is the sense of לשוח בשדה, and likewise (Genesis 28:11): ״ויפגע במקום״ — for the שיחה in the field is the פגיעה in the Place, and this is the sense of (Jeremiah 7:16): ״ואל תפגע בי״; (Job 21:15): ״ומה נועיל כי נפגע בו״. And all the actions are attributed to the pronoun, and go out to the Active One by the power of the Unique Name. And this is what Jeremiah said (Jeremiah 8:14): ״כי ה׳ אלהינו הדמנו וישקנו מי ראש כי חטאנו לה׳״ — לו, it says only לה׳; and understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:54.635691283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}